<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="theme-color" content="#142d4c"><meta name="description" content="Explore assistance programs available in Washington."><title>Washington Assistance Programs — American Aid Network</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/site.css"></head><body><?php require __DIR__ . "/../../includes/site-header.php"; ?><main><section class="state-page"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span>›</span><a href="/help/">Browse Programs</a><span>›</span><b>Washington</b></div><div class="state-intro"><div><h1>Assistance Programs in Washington</h1><p>11 programs, grouped by what you need help with. Each includes clear application guidance.</p></div><div><a class="button primary" href="/find/">Find my programs <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><small>Free · Private · Takes under 2 minutes</small></div></div><section class="program-group"><h2>Rent &amp; Housing Assistance</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>Aged, Blind, or Disabled (ABD) Cash Assistance</h3><p>ABD is a Washington cash program from DSHS for low-income adults who are 65 or older, blind, or likely to meet the Social Security disability standard. It pays a monthly cash grant while helping you apply for federal SSI, and it can connect you to the Housing and Essential Needs (HEN) program. Apply at washingtonconnection.org or by phone at 1-877-501-2233.</p><div><a href="/programs/aged-blind-or-disabled-abd-cash-assistance/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/aged-blind-or-disabled-abd-cash-assistance/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>Washington 211</h3><p>Dial 2-1-1 from any Washington phone, or call 1-877-211-9274, for free, confidential help finding local assistance with housing, utilities, food, healthcare, and more. Washington 211 is a statewide service with a database of thousands of local resources. You can also text 211WAOD to 898211 or search at wa211.org.</p><div><a href="/programs/washington-211/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/washington-211/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>Washington Apple Health (Medicaid)</h3><p>Apple Health is Washington&#39;s Medicaid program: free or low-cost health coverage for children, pregnant people, parents, older adults, people with disabilities, and low-income adults. Apply online at wahealthplanfinder.org, or call the Washington Healthplanfinder Customer Support Center at 1-855-923-4633. For coverage questions, the Health Care Authority line is 1-800-562-3022.</p><div><a href="/programs/washington-apple-health-medicaid/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/washington-apple-health-medicaid/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>Washington Legal Aid (CLEAR / Northwest Justice Project)</h3><p>CLEAR is Washington&#39;s toll-free legal aid intake line, run by the Northwest Justice Project, for low-income residents with civil, noncriminal problems like eviction, housing, family, and public benefits. Call 1-888-201-1014, Monday through Friday, 9:15am to 12:15pm. Residents 60 and older can call CLEAR*Sr at 1-888-387-7111. Free self-help guides are at washingtonlawhelp.org.</p><div><a href="/programs/washington-legal-aid-clear-northwest-justice-project/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/washington-legal-aid-clear-northwest-justice-project/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>Weatherization Assistance Program (Washington)</h3><p>Free home energy-efficiency work for income-eligible Washington households: insulation, air sealing, ventilation, and related repairs that lower future bills. The Department of Commerce funds the work through local agencies. Both homeowners and renters can qualify. Contact the weatherization agency serving your county to apply, since Commerce does not take applications directly.</p><div><a href="/programs/weatherization-assistance-program-washington/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/weatherization-assistance-program-washington/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Cash Assistance &amp; Benefits</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>Unemployment Benefits (Washington ESD)</h3><p>Temporary weekly payments if you lost work through no fault of your own, from the Washington Employment Security Department. File online through eServices at esd.wa.gov, which is the fastest way and open around the clock, or call the claims center at 1-800-318-6022. After you apply, you must file a weekly claim for each week to be paid.</p><div><a href="/programs/unemployment-benefits-washington-esd/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/unemployment-benefits-washington-esd/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>Washington TANF / WorkFirst (Cash Assistance)</h3><p>Temporary Assistance for Needy Families, TANF, is Washington&#39;s monthly cash assistance for low-income families with children. Most adults take part in WorkFirst, the state&#39;s employment program, while the cash steadies the household. Apply online at washingtonconnection.org or by phone at 1-877-501-2233, or at your local DSHS Community Services Office.</p><div><a href="/programs/washington-tanf-workfirst-cash-assistance/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/washington-tanf-workfirst-cash-assistance/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Food Assistance</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>Washington Basic Food (SNAP)</h3><p>Basic Food is Washington&#39;s name for SNAP: monthly food money on an EBT card you use like a debit card at most grocery stores. Apply online at washingtonconnection.org, which handles Basic Food, cash assistance, and other help on one application, or by phone at 1-877-501-2233, Monday through Friday. You can also apply at your local DSHS Community Services Office.</p><div><a href="/programs/washington-basic-food-snap/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/washington-basic-food-snap/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>Washington WIC</h3><p>WIC gives healthy food, breastfeeding support, nutrition education, and health referrals to pregnant and postpartum people, infants, and children up to age 5. Washington WIC runs through the Department of Health and local clinics. Find a clinic or apply by calling the WIC Cascades Support Line at 1-800-841-1410, or start at doh.wa.gov.</p><div><a href="/programs/washington-wic/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/washington-wic/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Utility Bill Help</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>Washington Energy Assistance (LIHEAP)</h3><p>LIHEAP helps low-income Washington households pay home heating and energy bills. The state Department of Commerce funds the program, but you apply through the local community action agency that serves your county, not through Commerce directly. Each agency sets its own appointment process, so find your local provider on the Commerce LIHEAP page and contact them to apply.</p><div><a href="/programs/washington-energy-assistance-liheap/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/washington-energy-assistance-liheap/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Debt &amp; Credit Help</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>Washington Working Families Tax Credit</h3><p>The Working Families Tax Credit is Washington&#39;s refundable cash credit, run by the Department of Revenue. For the 2025 credit it pays up to $335 with no qualifying children, $660 with one child, $995 with two, and $1,330 with three or more, with a $50 minimum for those who qualify. Apply for free at workingfamiliescredit.wa.gov after you file your federal return.</p><div><a href="/programs/washington-working-families-tax-credit/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/washington-working-families-tax-credit/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div></section></div></section></main><footer><div class="wrap footer-grid"><div><a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="American Aid Network home"><span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true"><span>★</span><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span>AMERICAN <b>AID</b><small>NETWORK</small></span></a><p>Clear, reliable guidance to assistance programs across America.</p><div class="verified">✓ Information from trusted sources</div></div><div><h4>FIND SUPPORT</h4><a href="/find/">Find help near me</a><a href="/help/">Browse by state</a><a href="/programs/">Program guides</a><a href="/#how-it-works">How it works</a></div><div><h4>ABOUT</h4><a href="/about/">Our mission</a><a href="/legal/contact/">Contact us</a><a href="/legal/privacy/">Privacy policy</a><a href="/legal/terms/">Terms of use</a></div></div><div class="wrap disclaimer">American Aid Network is an independent informational resource. We are not a government agency and do not administer benefit programs. Program details change; always confirm requirements with the official provider.<span>© 2026 American Aid Network</span></div></footer><script src="/assets/site.js" defer></script></body></html>